    "question": {
      "source_id": "unreconciled:step-q182517",
      "problem": "Find the missing values in the following truth table:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,(A∧B)∨¬(A∨¬B)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-3}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\n \n\nUsing your results, complete the following statement:\n\n$$\n(A∧B)∨¬(A∨¬B){{field-4}}A\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's solve for the missing values:\n\n- When $A≡\\text{T}$ and $B≡\\text{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A∧B)∨¬(A∨¬B) & ≡(\\text{T}∧\\text{T})∨¬(\\text{T}∨¬\\text{T}) \\\\  & ≡(\\text{T}∧\\text{T})∨¬(\\text{T}∨\\text{F}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}∨¬\\text{T} \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $A≡\\text{T}$ and $B≡\\text{F},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A∧B)∨¬(A∨¬B) & ≡(\\text{T}∧\\text{F})∨¬(\\text{T}∨¬\\text{F}) \\\\  & ≡(\\text{T}∧\\text{F})∨¬(\\text{T}∨\\text{T}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}∨¬\\text{T} \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}∨\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $A≡\\text{F}$ and $B≡\\text{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A∧B)∨¬(A∨¬B) & ≡(\\text{F}∧\\text{T})∨¬(\\text{F}∨¬\\text{T}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}∨¬\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}∨\\text{T} \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur completed table is shown below.\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,(A∧B)∨¬(A∨¬B)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\nTo determine whether $(A∧B)∨¬(A∨¬B)$ is logically equivalent to $A,$ we need to check whether their truth tables are equivalent.\n\nWe see that the columns for $(A∧B)∨¬(A∨¬B)$ and $A$ are different. They differ in the second and third rows. Therefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\n(A∧B)∨¬(A∨¬B)≢A.\n$$",
